  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read mcp-r1's write-up, SignalReadService.ReadAsync end to end, the plan caller, task 023's follow-up note; write the step dependency graph and the client thread-safety findings to notes/task-222-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Equivalence and single-row tests first (they pin today's output), plus a round-trip/latency harness on the fake.</step>
    <step order="3">(B) single-row read through the existing pipeline; wire the plan caller to it if it is ontology code, otherwise expose it for mcp-r1.</step>
    <step order="4">(D) bounded concurrency on the independent edges only.</step>
    <step order="5">Filtered tests (Signals, incl. baselines unchanged), full ArchTests, BFF build, publish-size delta; before/after round trips and simulated wall-clock.</step>
    <step order="6">PR to master; notes in notes/task-222-notes.md; tell the main session the single-row method's signature for mcp-r1.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Equivalence tests pass before and after: every fixture lane returns the same rows, order and content; contract baselines unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The single-row read returns exactly the lane's row for every visible Signal and not-found (no existence detail) for every Signal a lane rule hides; it issues no lane-wide Signal fetch (round-trip count test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With a fixed per-call latency fake, the lane read's wall-clock drops (numbers reported); concurrency degree is bounded and tested; a fault or cancellation in any branch surfaces as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build, filtered tests, full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Main session (with mcp-r1) measures show/plan and the Console worklist p95 on dev after the next dev BFF build.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>A speed-up needs a change to which identity performs a read, a change to any visibility rule or response, a schema change, unbounded concurrency, or the clients are not safe for concurrent use: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree (C:\wt222); PR to master; do not merge.</protocol>
